sentences.l:
And at dawn, very early, bathe and anoint him,
so that inside beside Telemachus of his meal he may take thought,
sitting in the hall;

Whoever is unkind himself and knows unkind things,
upon him all mortals call down pains hereafter
while he lives, but when he is dead they all mock him;

for not yet any man so prudent
of friendly strangers from far-off lands has come to my house
as you very eloquently prudent things all say;

just as at you these dogs here mock, all of them,
of whom the outrage and many shames now avoiding
you do not allow them to wash you;
